  "model_vision_findings": "Inspected all fourteen native/before/current full pages, 5% pixel diffs and complete heading/list crops at 150 DPI, including all ten before/current shifted-region crops and all thirty-two current cluster pairs. Ten suffix pages now match Word: numbered space/nothing bodies follow their actual markers, including (10) at x=131.638pt/128.582pt; Unicode bullet bodies start at x=115.933pt/112.877pt; zero-indent inline markers start at x=90pt and their bodies follow with a space or no gap. Wrapped first lines and all three physical lines match; hanging-list continuations retain x=126pt. Default 16pt body text matches native marker and body size/placement. All pages remain one Letter page with the heading, six case72 paragraphs or five case71 paragraphs, black text and punctuation. Cambria 14pt bold headings and 11pt/16pt regular body retain their native appearance. No fills, strokes/borders, hairlines <=1pt, rotation, italics, underline, clipping, overflow or page-order change appears. Two level-rPr probes still paint Cambria 11pt markers instead of declared Times New Roman/16pt; their wrong marker geometry, resulting body positions and vertical drift up to 18.921pt are tracked in #2100, including twenty font-case and eight size-case clusters. Two additional inline-format probes retain wrong Roman and ancestor labels under #2099, with four exact current raster IDs. All those fragments were re-inspected; none is approved as a renderer difference. Sub-material baseline drift <=0.276pt and pitch drift <=0.191pt on passing suffix pages remain under #1874. No other material deviation was found.",
